  "description": "A Victorian end of terrace three bedroom house, located in a highly desirable area around the corner from the centre of Summertown's shopping parade. No onward chain.\n\nAn attractive Victorian end of terraced house having been extended to provide generous living space arranged over 3 floors with a utility room in the basement.\n\nThe property comprises, entrance hall, lounge/diner with bay window, 'L' shaped kitchen/breakfast room, shower room, family/garden room. On the first floor there are 2 double bedrooms and a family bathroom. The loft has been converted to provide a generous double bedroom with Juliet Balcony and en-suite shower room. Outside there is a good sized rear garden with summer house and a horizontal small parking space to the front.\n\nAdditional Infomation to note: All mains services are connected. Ofcom checker confirms good indoor and outdoors mobile voice and data coverage. Superfast and Ultrafast broadband is available.\n\nNearby Summertown offers a mix of independent and high street shops, a range of cafes, restaurants and bars and an M&S Food store. There are also tennis courts, a swimming pool, health club, branch library and a mixture of state and private schooling including The Cherwell school, The Dragon and Headington. Oxford city centre is just a mile and a half away, served by a regular bus service. The John Radcliffe Hospital can be reached by bus from Marston Ferry Road.",
